abstract: >-
  Notes, measurements and verified code from a self-directed study
  of the multiplicative structure of the integers, starting from the
  division table. Contains independent re-derivations of known
  results (the sieve of Sundaram; the Hardy-Littlewood singular
  series; the explicit formula; Ramanujan-Fourier analysis of
  r-even functions; the Szego limit theorem; the Li-Sekatskii
  shifted Li coefficients; the major-arc expansion of the circle
  method; Buchstab's function and the wheel sieve), documented negative
  results and controls, and runnable verification scripts for every
  table and figure. A sixth paper probes the odd parity sector of the
  Connes-van Suijlekom Galerkin construction, reporting an exact
  finite identification on that sector, an unseeded reconstruction of
  the first ten zeta ordinates at four prime cutoffs, and a
  measurement of the Galerkin exponent against the archimedean cutoff
  that led the author of that construction to withdraw one of its
  stated mechanisms. No claim is made about the Riemann Hypothesis.
